{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I will bring you out from under the burdens of Egypt</b> — He promises them that He will bring them out from their land, and they will no longer bear the heavy load of their oppression." "<b>And I will deliver you from their bondage</b> — that they will not rule over them at all, to make of them in their place a labor-tax servant." "<b>And I will redeem you</b> — for He will bring judgments upon them until the Egyptians say, \"Behold, Israel is yours; with ransom we redeem our lives.\" For the meaning of גְּאֻלָּה is like the matter of a sale. And the meaning of <b>with an outstretched arm</b> is that His hand will be outstretched over them until He brings them out."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:31.573599053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}